n none; July and October fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Saranac Lake's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.19 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 37.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1954 (52.72 in); the driest, 1999 (29.10 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, 2 daily record lows"}}